// Σ_OS, THE LAYER'S PARAMETER (ADR 0093): what ι's terms need from an operating
// system and no LLVM instruction computes. Three operation symbols, each a
// header with no body: an OS layer that glues `llvm` defines each, under the
// same header, and a target that defines none of them is refused when it is
// loaded. Their contracts are what lang.oro's terms rely on, so they hold of
// every definition:
//
//   region     b fresh bytes, every one 0, or the trap (exhaustion): a table is
//              zero on creation (tables.md); never a null an access could reach
//   write_err  the bytes to standard error, answering whether they were written
//   exit       the process ends with the code; it never returns (ADR 0090). The
//              codes are 0..255, those every host reports the same way.
module llvm/os {
    fn region(b ∈ 0..2^63-1) (ptr)
    fn write_err(b ∈ Array(0..255)) (Bool)
    fn exit(code ∈ 0..255) (∅)
}
